text:
claire: FYI i opened PR #578 to merge the structured-output examples into the tool-calling migration guide: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/578

dave: glanced through. overall 👍. two asks: 1) include a validator-ready JSON Schema that people can paste into their CI, 2) show both named (object) and positional (array) arg examples.

ishan: also flag: some older docs still use `function_call` or `toolName`. we should standardize on `tool` and put a tiny compatibility note.

maria: agreed. i also want a short JS runtime snippet showing safe parsing + a caution about `confidence` not being a calibrated probability. marketing wanted a link to the evals guide we can use in the callout.

claire: dropping compact copy/paste schema so reviewers can yank it directly:```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {"oneOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "array"}]},
    "meta": {"type": "object"},
    "confidence": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

ishan: nice. for concrete validators add this enum example for common tools (`url_fetch`, `kv_get`) so teams can tighten schemas per tool:```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": {"type": "string", "enum": ["url_fetch", "kv_get"]},
    "args": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"type": "object", "properties": {"url": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["url"]},
        {"type": "array"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

maria: JS parse example for front-end folks:```js
const resp = await client.generate({ prompt });
const parsed = JSON.parse(resp.output); // model returns JSON string
const { tool, args } = parsed;
if (tool === 'url_fetch') { await fetch(args.url); }
```

dave: add a short compatibility snippet for older shape: "If you used `function_call.name`/`function_call.arguments`, map to `tool`/`args` (object or array)." Put it in a small note.

claire: done. also adding a 3-item migration checklist at top of the doc: 1) rename examples to `tool`/`args`, 2) paste validator schema or per-tool enum, 3) add redirects for any changed public paths.

snippet-bot: CI: snippet linter found one unreachable internal path in the migration doc (`/sdk/py/old-examples`). flagged for replacement.

ishan: replace with `/sdk/python/migration#tool-calls` and add a tiny `_redirects.yml` PR for the old path. marketing asked for redirects on public docs changes.

maria: i'll add the evals callout text: "Note: `confidence` is model-provided and advisory only; do not treat it as a calibrated probability. Use domain heuristics or your evals to gate automated actions. See /guides/evals for details."

dave: ok final asks: include an explicit positional-args example for `kv_get` (e.g., "args": ["my-key"]) and add `additionalProperties: false` to the schemas so validators catch typos.

claire: adding both. will push the changes and request a final review from @dave. target merge by EOD tomorrow. thanks all :shipit:
